{"ts":"2026-08-13T21:47:02.765Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2a00cb64a3a7c61d1591525b","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-brief-bjll"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The brief reported the side a merge requested as the side it kept, which under stable value order is the opposite of what happened"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Every merge-decision renderer interpolated the receipt side directly, printing kept ours or kept theirs. pm-cli GH-974 established that a receipt can record a requested side while retaining the other branch value, because the item driver settles scalar conflicts by stable value order rather than by branch. Reproduced against a real two-branch merge under 2026.8.13: the receipt records requested_preference ours and conflict_resolution stable_value_order, while the decision retains the theirs value and discards the ours value. The brief therefore told an agent its peer edit lost when the reverse had happened, reintroducing one layer up the contradiction upstream had just removed. The phrasing now keys off the resolution contract rather than the recorded side, and says kept by stable value order when no branch won."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["correctness","merge"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:47:02.765Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T21:47:02.765Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"f174c2a49fd6fc9ff50398fa0721e9ad6813c61d3e544661bb59585ce18cfa02","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
